# Integration budget: nominal fastest period 8ns, reserve 0.5ns.
# Only reviewed registered Gray -> first synchronization stage.
# New CCR/route/exception/max-skew and same-clock follow-on evidence required.
# REVIEW CANDIDATE ONLY: new compile/map/PNR + CCR + exception/max-skew report required.
# No clock-group cut; no stage-2, reset/async pins or PHY exceptions.
# Gray source contract: registered reflected Gray, at most one bit changes per source step.
# Fastest participating nominal clock period 8ns; use 8ns max physical data+setup budget.
# Existing 36-bit old-route coverage is recorded in findings.json.
# Physical source-period/jitter guard and MTBF remain integration signoff requirements.
# rptr -> wrptr1: expect exactly 9 connected crossing paths.
